r older. The audit flags the `approved_first_review` data problem instead of hiding it. It also says that every agent in the period, auditor included, is the same model family, which weakens its independence.\n\n**Weak points (not blocking):**\n- **Unverified numbers:** I couldn't recount the figures. My two greps for an outcome field in records 77 to 96 found nothing, so I didn't confirm the 14 done / 6 blocked split or the $27.12 total.\n- **Placeholder figures:**\n  - **O1 and TEP-0009:** O1 says the four placeholder blocks cost \"$4.36, 22% of the period's spend\", and TEP-0009 repeats the $4.36. The audit's own per-packet costs don't support it. For PKT-0080, 0081 and 0086 it gives $1.44 + $0.97 + $0.77 = $3.18, which would leave PKT-0083 at about $1.18. But PKT-0083 is also listed as an external block in the TEP-0001 verdict.\n  - **The 4-of-20 baseline:** TEP-0009's hypothesis uses \"4 of 20\" as its baseline. Strictly, only 3 of those blocks are placeholder or repeated-failure blocks, because PKT-0083 was blocked on a wrong target path.\n- **Wrong label on the blocked-friction gap:** the period has 6 blocked records, but only 4 packets ended blocked; PKT-0068 and PKT-0078 were later done. So \"0/4\" is right, but the gap is labelled as TEP-0004's, while the scoreboard already shows TEP-0004 as met on the fields it targets.\n\nAUD-5 should check the TEP-0009 baseline again before using it.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Complete AUD-4 with the comparison to AUD-3, hypothesis verdicts, a \"what not to change\" section and two well-formed TEPs; scope, contract and TEP-0004 conditions met","ttft_ms":2152,"type":"result","duration_ms":24232,"uuid":"11c1a872-26d3-4f2f-8149-13c3c14614ad","ttft_stream_ms":817,"time_to_request_ms":317,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":203,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":23,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":10,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":3,"e